resources.string:
The screening mechanism fundamentally relies on triggering carrier "Call Forwarding on Busy":

1. When an incoming call arrives, CallScreeningService checks the list and active time window;
2. If matched, the call is rejected immediately, returning a "busy" signal to the cellular network;
3. The carrier network detects the busy state and triggers your configured busy forwarding;
4. The call is automatically routed to your target number (e.g. secondary phone, landline) or plays carrier prompt tones (out of service, powered off, etc.).

★ All forwarding is executed on the carrier network side. The app does not place a second call, making it secure, battery-friendly, and latency-free.
